                <pb facs="0472" n="378" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg378"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.001/54: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Reber</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-12-03T14:00:00-00:44">December 3, 1930—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 3:15 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>169. President King has just informed me that he will resign this afternoon at 3
                    o’clock. Edwin Barclay, the Secretary of State and lawful successor, will assume
                    the Presidency.</p>
                <pb facs="0473" n="379" xml:id="pg379"/>
                <p>President added that he was compelled to resign on account of the opposition to
                    his reform program and made no further comment on the Secretary’s
                    memorandum.</p>
                <p>Barclay is openly anti-white and opposed to the International Commission’s
                    recommendations. I shall await instructions before calling upon the new
                    President.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Reber</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
